# Toolchain version pins, declared once. Everything that installs or checks a
# version reads this file instead of carrying its own copy:
#
#   mobile-bake/scripts/*.sh        bake-image.sh ships this file with the
#                                   payload and bake.sh drops it next to the
#                                   scripts in the guest, which source it
#   android-image/Dockerfile        every pin is a default-less ARG; the
#                                   builder passes this file as --build-arg
#                                   (bootstrap.sh does, see README for manual
#                                   builds) and the image keeps a copy at
#                                   /etc/ghrunner-versions.env for
#                                   verify-toolchain.sh
#   mise run runner:pins            regenerates the "synced" block from a
#                                   your-org/your-app checkout with
#                                   derive-versions.sh and diffs it against
#                                   this file
#
# Format: KEY=value lines and comments only. No quoting, no expansion - it is
# sourced by bash, sed'ed into --build-arg flags, and read back by grep.
#
# A change here changes what the images contain, so bump BAKE_IMAGE_NAME in
# the affected bake.env (and re-bake / re-provision) when you move a pin.

# --- Synced from your-org/your-app ------------------------------------
# derive-versions.sh reads each of these off the app repo; `mise run
# runner:pins` shows the drift. Edit here deliberately, never auto-bump: the
# job workflow installs Node/EAS itself (setup-node, expo-github-action), so
# an image pin that lags only costs a download, while a pin that leads can
# build something the app never tested.
#
# install-build action, setup-node node-version (Homebrew installs the
# matching node@<major> formula on the macOS image; the Linux image is the
# exact node:<version> base).
NODE_VERSION=22.23.4
# package.json packageManager. Also names the checked-in yarn release the
# prime runs (.yarn/releases/yarn-<ver>.cjs).
YARN_VERSION=3.8.1
# eas-build-ship action, setup-java java-version. Temurin on macOS, OpenJDK on
# Linux; Maestro runs on it too.
JAVA_VERSION=17
# yarn.lock resolution of `expo` (major) and `react-native`. EXPO_SDK selects
# the template the Linux image's Gradle seed builds; REACT_NATIVE_VERSION is
# where derive-versions.sh finds the Android toolchain catalog below.
EXPO_SDK=57
REACT_NATIVE_VERSION=0.86.3
# app.config.ts compileSdkVersion (targetSdk is a manifest value and needs no
# platform installed). Cross-checked against React Native's catalog.
ANDROID_COMPILE_SDK=36
# react-native/gradle/libs.versions.toml: buildTools and ndkVersion. RN's
# ReactAndroid and Expo's root Gradle plugin both configure the NDK from it,
# and a real build logs "- ndk: <version>" while configuring; 20-prime-repo.sh
# compares that line against this pin.
ANDROID_BUILD_TOOLS=36.0.0
ANDROID_NDK=27.1.12297006
# gradle-wrapper.properties inside the Expo prebuild template
# (node_modules/expo/template.tgz -> android/gradle/wrapper). `expo prebuild`
# writes exactly this into the generated project, so it is what every job's
# ./gradlew fetches; 15-prime-tools.sh pre-places it and 20-prime-repo.sh
# prunes any other dist. A wrong value here wastes ~150MB of image, never a
# job (v6 shipped a stale 8.14.3-all this way).
GRADLE_VERSION=9.3.1
GRADLE_DIST_TYPE=bin

# --- Observed from real builds, declared nowhere in mobile-apps ------------
# Not derivable, so derive-versions.sh leaves these alone. Move them only
# with a re-bake and a green Android build.
#
# android-35 shipped on the validated v4 macOS image; kept so a dependency
# that still compiles against it does not trade a baked platform for an
# in-job download. Braze's Expo module has been seen requesting Build Tools
# 35.0.0; only the Linux image pre-installs it (the macOS bake does not, and
# AGP fetches a missing build-tools on demand once licenses are accepted).
ANDROID_LEGACY_PLATFORM=35
ANDROID_LEGACY_BUILD_TOOLS=35.0.0
# A second NDK the Linux image carries because Expo Updates was seen selecting
# 27.0 while the root project selects 27.1. Not in any Expo package source at
# SDK 55 or 57 (expo-modules-core inherits the root ndkVersion, expo-updates
# sets none); drop it once a Linux image build no longer asks for it.
ANDROID_EXPO_NDK=27.0.12077973
# The Android Gradle Plugin's default CMake, which the build neither declares
# nor logs. 20-prime-repo.sh confirms it after the warm build from the cmake
# binary path recorded in the generated project's .cxx/ dir.
ANDROID_CMAKE=3.22.1

# --- Runner infrastructure: moved on this repo's cadence -------------------
# mobile-apps states minimums for some of these (scripts/doctor.sh, eas.json
# cli.version); `mise run runner:pins` checks the pins still satisfy them.
#
# Maestro CLI. The installer takes the newest otherwise, which made v5
# unreproducible. 2.10.0 is what the 18/18-green E2E suite ran on (Sep 2026);
# bump deliberately, with a suite run.
MAESTRO_VERSION=2.10.0
# EAS CLI on the Linux image (the job's expo-github-action may install its own
# on top; pinning that action is a mobile-apps change).
EAS_CLI_VERSION=23.0.0
# Android command-line tools zip (the sdkmanager bootstrap) for the Linux
# image. The macOS image gets its sdkmanager from the Homebrew cask instead.
ANDROID_COMMAND_LINE_TOOLS=15859902
ANDROID_COMMAND_LINE_TOOLS_SHA256=4e4c464f145a7512b57d088ac6c278c03c9eea610886b35a5e0804e74eedf583
# gcloud CLI on the Linux image, from Google's versioned tarball. The macOS
# bake pulls the rapid channel's current tarball (unversioned URL) and records
# what it got in the bake log.
GCLOUD_VERSION=581.0.0
GCLOUD_AMD64_SHA256=deffdbe82ca6e3d19ffb291d063a651488e04e1b33799b5a238e4b5c6784e3c6
GCLOUD_ARM64_SHA256=22cfc09888525c6daadb8764388ce14e6c26baf80ab07938eacb08c2b4ae64c9
# Cloudflare WARP .deb for the Linux image (headless daemon + CLI only). The
# checksums come from Cloudflare's signed Bookworm index. macOS uses the cask.
WARP_VERSION=2026.7.1377.0
WARP_AMD64_SHA256=95d33c2b4fc42f21c204981c51470a6a679d618fb0b78ee64bdd0db142230c55
WARP_ARM64_SHA256=7d97a4affa74f7814e94733d6241f0df5186d2bb80e5a8548eaa4a769d57c28e
